#orderi429@gmail.com
This project implements a full version of the Coup board game in C++ using OOP principles. It includes a graphical interface with SFML and unit
tests using the doctest framework. The game supports 2–6 players, each with a special role and unique abilities. All actions follow the rules
of the game strictly and invalid moves are blocked or throw exceptions. Memory usage was tested using Valgrind and no leaks were found.

If a player cannot perform an action (due to being blocked or not having enough coins), the button for that action does not appear in the GUI.

The special ability of the Spy is implemented in a way that lets them see all players' coin counts at the start of their
turn, and choose which player to block from using arrest.

main.cpp runs the game using SFML and allows all players to play on one screen.

Game.cpp and Game.hpp implement the game logic including the players list, the current turn, last action, coin pool, and undo logic.

Player.hpp and Player.cpp define a base Player class with common logic for all roles. Each role inherits from Player and overrides 
relevant methods to implement its unique behavior.

Roles include Governor, Spy, Baron, General, Judge, and Merchant. Each role class has its own file and logic for its special rules.

PlayerFactory creates players with the correct role.

test.cpp includes unit tests using doctest. The tests check every player role and every game action including invalid cases.

Makefile automates build and test:

    make Main – builds and runs the demo game
    
    make test – runs the unit tests

    make valgrind – checks for memory leaks

    make clean – removes compiled files
